  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules keep the 5% per-model failure benchmark but remove any obligation to stop sales above it, which protects Northwind's 6.2% Hearth 10. The 24-month new-unit shut-off delay and 6-year retrofit window also favour Northwind, whose share of shut-off-capable units is only 38%. The 8/100k mandatory recall trigger with no transition is the one provision that bites Halcyon's 9.9/100k Ember 8, and the 36-month suppression delay is a modest concession to Halcyon."
 },
